From 1fefc92cbc4a8c4950fffde94b385a79ce1166d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evox95 <evox95@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 17:24:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add @sidebar_sort option for start-time ordering
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add an opt-in `@sidebar_sort` tmux option controlling the agent list order:

- `repo` (default) keeps today's behavior — panes grouped by git
  repository, groups sorted alphabetically by name.
- `started` (aliases `start`/`age`/`oldest`) renders a single flat list
  of every session ordered by start time, oldest first. Repo group
  headers and their spawn buttons are suppressed. Sessions without a
  reported `started_at` sort last, tiebroken by pane id for determinism.

Ordering is centralized in `AppState::flat_started_order`, consumed by
both the row renderer and the click/scroll row-target builder so the
drawn rows and the row map can never disagree.

Adds unit tests for the option parser and the ordering, plus flat-vs-
grouped render snapshots. Documents the option in the tmux-options
reference and the config header.
